# Blog Content

- Blog posts live in `src/content/blog` as Markdown files. The filename becomes the URL slug.
- Keep post frontmatter complete: `title`, `description`, `date`, and `tags`.
- Treat `src/content/blog/manifest.ts` as generated output from `scripts/generate-blog-manifest.mjs`.
- After adding, deleting, renaming, or editing blog Markdown frontmatter, regenerate the manifest before verification.
- Keep Markdown rendering build-time and trusted. Do not wire arbitrary user-submitted HTML into `MarkdownArticle`.
- Preserve SEO expectations: blog list/post metadata should use the post title, description, date, and tags consistently.
